  "id": "tsh",
  "term": "TSH",
  "definition": "TSH, or thyroid-stimulating hormone, is a key hormone in the hypothalamic-pituitary-thyroid axis and is highly sensitive to changes in thyroid balance. Because it often shifts before FT3 or FT4 do, it is commonly used as a primary screening marker of thyroid dysfunction in clinical and research settings.",
